#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:199
msgid ""
"Returns the launch annotation ``key`` recorded by T.Kernel (e.g. "
"``cluster_dims``), or ``default`` when it was not given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:206
msgid ""
"Returns the cluster dimensions as ``[x, y, z]``. A launch without "
"``cluster_dims`` has clusters of a single program, i.e. ``[1, 1, 1]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:213
msgid ""
"Returns the number of programs per cluster (product of the cluster "
"dimensions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:219
msgid ""
"Returns the index of the cluster the current program belongs to along "
"``dim``, in program-space arithmetic: ``block_id // cluster_dims[dim]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:222
msgid ""
"A cluster is a ``cluster_dims``-shaped tile of the grid, so this is the same "
"on every target (clusterIdx on CUDA, a group of consecutive programs "
"elsewhere) and stays consistent with threadblock swizzling, which permutes "
"the grid at cluster granularity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:237
msgid ""
"Returns the number of clusters along ``dim``: ``ceil(grid_extent / "
"cluster_dims[dim])``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:251
msgid "Returns the block indices from the topmost frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:265
msgid "Returns the total number of threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:270
msgid ""
"Mark ``func`` as a launch factory: a callable used as ``with func(...)`` to "
"open a kernel launch. Every dialect's ``Kernel`` (and ``ClusterKernel``) "
"carries this mark so the eager JIT rewriter can find the launch regardless "
"of which dialect or alias the user went through."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:282
msgid ""
"The well-known launch annotations are normalized here; any other keyword a "
"dialect forwards is recorded verbatim on the launch block for that backend's "
"pipeline to consume. Dialects, not this function, decide which keywords "
"exist: they only forward what their own ``Kernel`` signature declares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:293
msgid ""
"This is the target-neutral launch: the part every backend shares. Backend "
"dialects offer their own ``T.Kernel`` with the launch annotations that "
"backend understands, e.g. ``tilelang.cuda.language.Kernel(..., "
"threads=128)``; ``tilelang.language`` is the CUDA dialect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:298
msgid ""
"Extent of the grid along each axis (1-3 dimensions). The launch yields one "
"program index per axis (``blockIdx`` on CUDA, the outer loop on CPU, the "
"core index on an NPU)."
msgstr ""

